# Admin

`/admin` sits outside the wallet layout. `openAdmin()` in `lib/admin.server.ts` reads the Better Auth session and allows the visit only when that Google email is in the `ADMIN_EMAILS` env var (comma-separated). Comparison ignores case and surrounding spaces. Read it as `process.env.ADMIN_EMAILS`. An empty value lets nobody in. A signed-out visit shows the sign-in screen and returns to `/admin`. A signed-in account that is not on the list gets the missing page.

Do not import `lib/admin.server.ts` from a client component. The account menu learns about access through `AdminAccess`, a boolean passed from the server. The email list stays on the server.

The page reads counts and recent accounts from `profile`, `wait_alert`, `push_subscription`, and `schedule`, plus the camera rows and the cached CBP snapshot. Recent accounts include how that person said they found the app, when they answered, and the page totals those answers. Each recent account also shows its usage from `usage_event`, totalled per account in SQL by `readUsageTotals()` (`lib/usage.server.ts`): counts of days, questions, alerts, alarms, and saves, plus when it was last active. The Usage section totals those across accounts. The kinds and their labels live in `lib/usage.ts`, which is client-safe. The page does not write those tables, except `ensureProfile` for the admin on that visit. It does not show push endpoints.
